{"data": [{"author_id": "1499580477975535619", "conversation_id": "2117343192245064004", "created_at": "2026-11-03T00:55:25.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117420350216536411"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 12, "id": "1573399256836309009", "start": 0, "username": "kimmonismus"}]}, "id": "2117420350216536411", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 6, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117343192245064004", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus next step - astra edits its own weights and we call it a patch release", "url": "https://x.com/sentimentGod/status/2117420350216536411"}, {"author_id": "2029201612493950976", "conversation_id": "2117343192245064004", "created_at": "2026-11-03T00:48:25.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117418588307079649"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 12, "id": "1573399256836309009", "start": 0, "username": "kimmonismus"}, {"end": 134, "id": "895332160130891776", "start": 124, "username": "neuralink"}]}, "id": "2117418588307079649", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 9, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117343192245064004", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus Guess this is true for human brain also. Change some neurons here and there and we could all be math geniuses. @neuralink", "url": "https://x.com/makeofsense/status/2117418588307079649"}, {"author_id": "648863", "conversation_id": "2117343192245064004", "created_at": "2026-11-03T00:47:03.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117418243044585952"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 12, "id": "1573399256836309009", "start": 0, "username": "kimmonismus"}]}, "id": "2117418243044585952", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 6, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117343192245064004", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus We have a real recursive improving loop only if the modified model surpasses the modifying model on the same task. Only then can we test whether an improvement ceiling exists.", "url": "https://x.com/xone_4/status/2117418243044585952"}, {"author_id": "1584977655094513664", "conversation_id": "2117343192245064004", "created_at": "2026-11-03T00:43:42.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117417399011934368"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 12, "id": "1573399256836309009", "start": 0, "username": "kimmonismus"}]}, "id": "2117417399011934368", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 10, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117343192245064004", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus If this is not bulllshit...", "url": "https://x.com/zack80349105/status/2117417399011934368"}, {"author_id": "1671136128953638914", "conversation_id": "2117343192245064004", "created_at": "2026-11-03T00:30:12.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117414003471487367"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 12, "id": "1573399256836309009", "start": 0, "username": "kimmonismus"}]}, "id": "2117414003471487367", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 7, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117343192245064004", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus The 0.016% is what really blows my mind. If targeted weight edits can reliably fix reasoning failures, improving AI might start to look more like debugging software than retraining an entire model. That's a fascinating direction.", "url": "https://x.com/DimmensCK/status/2117414003471487367"}, {"author_id": "2953739684", "conversation_id": "2117343192245064004", "created_at": "2026-11-03T00:30:06.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117413977605152821"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 12, "id": "1573399256836309009", "start": 0, "username": "kimmonismus"}]}, "id": "2117413977605152821", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117343192245064004", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus The part that stands out to me is the scale of the edit: 0.016% of weights, no gradients.\n\nIf this holds up, the first practical use is probably debugging small open models, not self-improvement of frontier ones.", "url": "https://x.com/AzrianoY1/status/2117413977605152821"}, {"author_id": "2994713035", "conversation_id": "2117343192245064004", "created_at": "2026-11-03T00:22:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117411938091278724"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 12, "id": "1573399256836309009", "start": 0, "username": "kimmonismus"}]}, "id": "2117411938091278724", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117343192245064004", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus If it replicates, the governance problem is as big as the capability. Editing 0.016% of weights leaves no training run or dataset to audit, and most model change-control today only logs fine-tunes. Labs will need to diff weights, not just track jobs.", "url": "https://x.com/CHMUQADDASNAWAZ/status/2117411938091278724"}, {"author_id": "236841866", "conversation_id": "2117343192245064004", "created_at": "2026-11-03T00:16:42.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117410605149856107"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 12, "id": "1573399256836309009", "start": 0, "username": "kimmonismus"}]}, "id": "2117410605149856107", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 5, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117343192245064004", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus This is basically having LLMs do crispr on other LLMs", "url": "https://x.com/jeremiahscholl/status/2117410605149856107"}, {"author_id": "1628751379710853120", "conversation_id": "2117343192245064004", "created_at": "2026-11-03T00:14:38.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117410087102730633"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 12, "id": "1573399256836309009", "start": 0, "username": "kimmonismus"}]}, "id": "2117410087102730633", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117343192245064004", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus can you fucking read? this entire thing is bullshit, did you even open the blog?\n\n90% of  your posts are late and retarded", "url": "https://x.com/GgHemeleh/status/2117410087102730633"}, {"author_id": "1711973911775047680", "conversation_id": "2117343192245064004", "created_at": "2026-11-02T23:55:41.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117405315713175731"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 12, "id": "1573399256836309009", "start": 0, "username": "kimmonismus"}]}, "id": "2117405315713175731", "lang": "en", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117343192245064004", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus Maybe this is the first step for RSI ...", "url": "https://x.com/xblooddyx/status/2117405315713175731"}, {"author_id": "1229624634707935234", "conversation_id": "2117343192245064004", "created_at": "2026-11-02T23:51:03.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117404148819796073"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 9, "id": "835970218966986753", "start": 0, "username": "doghutty"}, {"end": 22, "id": "1573399256836309009", "start": 10, "username": "kimmonismus"}]}, "id": "2117404148819796073", "la